==Trivia==
The illustration rare print of this card features a [[Water Stone]], a [[Thunder Stone]], and a [[Fire Stone]]—which are used to evolve Eevee into {{p|Vaporeon}}, {{p|Jolteon}}, and {{p|Flareon}} respectively—as well as a [[Poké Toy]].

===Origin===
*This card's standard illustrations are pulled from a variety of cards across the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]]:
**The 206/226 print's illustration was first featured on {{TCG ID|Ultra Prism|Eevee|104}} from the {{TCG|Ultra Prism}} expansion;
**The 207/226 print's illustration was first featured on {{TCG ID|Cosmic Eclipse|Eevee|167}} from the {{TCG|Cosmic Eclipse}} expansion;
**The 208/226 print's illustration was first featured on {{TCG ID|Lost Thunder|Eevee|155}} from the {{TCG|Lost Thunder}} expansion.
*Both this card and the Cosmic Eclipse print have the {{m|Tackle}} attack; this is a [[move]] in the [[Pokémon games]] that {{p|Eevee}} can learn.
*This card's [[Pokédex]] entry comes from {{g|Scarlet}}.

